# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_hostile_path_poison.py" "HOSTILE PATH POISON GATE: PASS" "Never-crash: a hostile changed-file path (over the gate's 1024 target_path cap, or carrying a NUL byte) is dropped before the claim loop -- it can no longer poison a whole PR's event" "NEVER-CRASH path poison guard. The gate caps a claim's target_path at 1024 chars (db/schema/20_core.sql claim_path_len; db/schema/30_gate.sql _place_claim RAISEs 23514 'target_path too long (max 1024)' above it) and psycopg2 refuses a string literal carrying a NUL (0x00) byte. The brain (webhook.py) passed each changed-file path STRAIGHT from GitHub's Files API to declare_claim / act_for_claim, and _code_paths (webhook_handlers.py) -- the shared filter every path flows through (PR claims, push branch lanes, the landing record) -- did NFC + dedup + non-code drop but NEVER bounded path length nor stripped a NUL. So a PR that adds ONE file whose path exceeds 1024 chars (a legitimate, attacker-craftable filename -- git allows paths to 4096 bytes and GitHub's API returns the real name) made the per-path claim loop RAISE mid-event: the exception ESCAPED handle_event, ABORTED the shared per-event transaction (the PR coordinated NOTHING = a false clear / silent miss), and re-crashed on every GitHub redelivery = a POISON event (same class as the _bounded_claim_id collision guard, but on the unbounded target_path itself). A crafted over-length / NUL filename in any single PR file thus SILENTLY SUPPRESSED Veripsa on that whole PR. FIX (recall-safe, content-free): _code_paths now DROPS a path the gate could never accept -- one whose NFC form exceeds _PATH_LEN_CAP (1024, measured AFTER NFC since normalization can change length) or that contains a NUL. Dropping one pathological path (a clean miss on that file, the REST of the PR still analyzed) is strictly safer than crashing + poisoning the event. Valid input is UNCHANGED -- a real source path is far under 1024 chars and carries no NUL. The gate proves UNIT (drop over-cap/NUL, KEEP a valid sibling and a path exactly AT the 1024 cap, no-op on a realistic list) and END-TO-END (the LIVE handle_event over a shared non-autocommit txn like the live processor: a hostile-path PR does NOT raise, the txn stays USABLE = no silent poison, and the PR's valid sibling file IS still claimed)." "Hostile-path never-crash: a PR whose changed files include a >1024-char path and a NUL-bearing path runs through the live handle_event without raising, leaves the shared per-event transaction usable (no aborted-txn poison), still claims the valid sibling file, and _code_paths drops exactly the two hostile paths while keeping a path EXACTLY at the 1024 cap and a realistic list unchanged -- proving a crafted filename can no longer suppress Veripsa on a whole PR or poison every redelivery." 20
